    "_uid": "7fa556d2-a997-07bc-1772-f50433011e53",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "25ae3060-c69a-4c08-15a4-38bf962db21f",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Highlighting the challenges that nurses routinely encounter in the patient area of the emergency department, five stations were designed for certain priority skills in this boot camp. These included managing mechanical ventilators, managing portable ventilators, managing and handling CVC lines and obtaining CVP, performing ostomy care when required, and understanding the preparation required for intubation. Each station lasted for 45 minutes, allowing each participant to practise all of their skills as thoroughly as possible. A total of 24 nurses participated in this workshop. Under the supervision of experienced instructors, they gained invaluable skills and knowledge that will surely guide their future practical clinical experiences. The workshop helped to increase conﬁdence in assessment, decision making, prioritisation and critical thinking skills among the participants.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
